Package: skyscapeR
Type: Package
Title: Data Analysis and Visualization for Skyscape Archaeology
Version: 2.0.9015
Authors@R: c(
    person("Fabio", "Silva", email = "fsilva@stonexsky.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Billy", "Finnimore", email = "billy.finnimore@hotmail.co.uk",
           role = "ctb"),
    person("Victor", "Reijs", role = "ctb"),
    person("Rita", "Gautschy", role = "ctb"))
Maintainer: Fabio Silva <fsilva@stonexsky.com>
Description: Investigate how archaeological sites and structures relate to
    the landscape and sky. Reduce field measurements, reconstruct local
    horizons from surveys and elevation models, and propagate measurement
    uncertainty into distributions of astronomical declination. Explore celestial
    positions, visibility and seasonal events at modern and prehistoric epochs,
    visualise the sky above a site horizon, and compare orientation distributions
    with random or specified null models (Silva 2020 <doi:10.1016/j.jas.2020.105138>,
    Silva and Lomsdalen 2025 <doi:10.1007/s12520-025-02208-4>).
URL: https://github.com/stonexsky/skyscapeR,
        https://stonexsky.github.io/skyscapeR/
BugReports: https://github.com/stonexsky/skyscapeR/issues
Depends: R (>= 4.1), swephR
Imports: parallel, methods, oce (>= 1.8-4), utils, tools, stats,
        graphics, grDevices, zoo
Additional_repositories: https://rstub.r-universe.dev
